        <item>
            <title>0.3.0</title>
            <pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 01:21:36 +0000</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/thaw-app/Floe/releases/tag/0.3.0</link>
            <sparkle:version>5</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.3.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<p><strong>macOS 26 and later · Build 5</strong></p>
<div class="markdown-alert markdown-alert-note"><p class="markdown-alert-title"><svg data-component="Octicon" class="octicon octicon-info mr-2" viewBox="0 0 16 16" version="1.1" width="16" height="16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z"></path></svg>Note</p><p><strong>Contributing is easier now</strong></p>
<p><a href="https://github.com/thaw-app/Floe/blob/development/AGENTS.md">AGENTS.md</a> tells AI coding agents, and the people using them, how to contribute to Floe. <a href="https://github.com/thaw-app/Floe/blob/development/docs/CODING_STANDARDS.md">CODING_STANDARDS.md</a> says how code and text are written here. Read both before you open a pull request, whether you write the change yourself or with an agent.</p>
<p>If an AI helps with your change, see the <a href="https://github.com/thaw-app/.github/blob/main/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md#ai-assisted-contributions">AI-assisted contributions</a> section of our contribution guidelines first: you stay responsible for the change and must be able to explain it, and the tool's terms have to let you contribute its output.</p>
</div>
<p>Floe's Settings now share their controls and pages with Thaw through <a href="https://github.com/thaw-app/ThawUI">ThawUI</a>, so the two apps look and behave more alike.</p>
<h3>New</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>File search finds what's in iCloud Drive</strong>, and shows it under that name. With Fast file search on, macOS may ask once for access to iCloud Drive (<a href="https://github.com/thaw-app/Floe/issues/59" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/thaw-app/Floe/issues/59/hovercard">#59</a>).</li>
</ul>
<h3>Changed</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>A slider sets the search field's corners</strong>, from square to fully round, in place of the three shapes. The shape you had stays as it was, and an older Floe syncing from another Mac keeps working.</li>
<li><strong>More text follows your Mac's text size</strong>, in the calculator, files, clipboard, Ask AI, Markdown and extension views. Some corners in these views and the note editor's toolbar icons change by a point or two to match the rest of the app.</li>
<li><strong>The toolbar names each Settings page</strong>, in place of the large title at the top, as in Thaw. Each group of search results has a heading like the sidebar's.</li>
<li><strong>About sits in the middle of its page</strong>, and its menu leaves out any link a build doesn't have.</li>
<li><strong>A keyboard shortcut macOS already uses keeps the recording going</strong>, so you can type another one straight away.</li>
<li><strong>The sidebar scrolls to the current page when Settings opens</strong>, and with Differentiate Without Color on, the selected row gets a ring.</li>
<li><strong>Numbered steps in the release notes keep their numbers.</strong></li>
</ul>
<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>What's New shows the latest releases.</strong> It was reading an older copy of the changelog that stopped at 0.1.0.</li>
<li><strong>A link in the release notes opens only if it is https</strong>, and a page that isn't the changelog, such as a Wi-Fi sign-in page, no longer replaces the saved notes.</li>
<li><strong>A saved keyboard shortcut with an impossible key is dropped</strong> when settings load, so registering it can't cause a crash.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Contributors</h3>
<ul>
<li><a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/matthrz/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/matthrz">@matthrz</a> asked to search iCloud Drive (<a href="https://github.com/thaw-app/Floe/issues/59" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/thaw-app/Floe/issues/59/hovercard">#59</a>).</li>
</ul>]]></description>
